1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:01,790
One clever teacher,

2
00:00:01,790 --> 00:00:03,390
or a whole school hall?

3
00:00:03,390 --> 00:00:05,300
Which works faster?

4
00:00:05,537 --> 00:00:07,347
Nvidia's famous chips are called

5
00:00:07,347 --> 00:00:08,487
GPUs,

6
00:00:08,487 --> 00:00:10,527
graphics processing units.

7
00:00:10,527 --> 00:00:11,457
They were first made to

8
00:00:11,457 --> 00:00:13,337
draw video games.

9
00:00:13,592 --> 00:00:15,322
An ordinary computer brain,

10
00:00:15,322 --> 00:00:16,552
a CPU,

11
00:00:16,552 --> 00:00:17,912
is like one very clever

12
00:00:17,912 --> 00:00:18,772
teacher,

13
00:00:18,772 --> 00:00:21,242
solving sums one after another.

14
00:00:21,242 --> 00:00:22,392
A GPU is like a

15
00:00:22,392 --> 00:00:24,442
whole school hall of pupils,

16
00:00:24,442 --> 00:00:26,412
each solving one small sum,

17
00:00:26,412 --> 00:00:28,292
all at the same time.

18
00:00:28,534 --> 00:00:29,754
And it turns out AI

19
00:00:29,754 --> 00:00:31,574
learns in a similar way:

20
00:00:31,574 --> 00:00:33,234
by doing billions and billions

21
00:00:33,234 --> 00:00:35,294
of small multiplications.

22
00:00:35,294 --> 00:00:36,194
So the chip built for

23
00:00:36,194 --> 00:00:37,954
games became the chip that

24
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:39,934
helps teach AI.

25
00:00:40,177 --> 00:00:42,227
Which finishes first: one friend

26
00:00:42,227 --> 00:00:43,367
with twenty sums,

27
00:00:43,367 --> 00:00:44,677
or twenty friends with one

28
00:00:44,677 --> 00:00:45,900
sum each?

29
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:47,150
Watch the full episode on

30
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:47,870
TheOneApp,

31
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:49,200
Explored.

32
00:00:49,411 --> 00:00:51,571
Now you know!
